            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Studies have demonstrated that a pattern in precipitation change emerges in a warmer climate, with more severe drought conditions over the western Sahel and an increase in precipitation over the central Sahel (Fontaine et al. 2011; Monerie et al. 2012, 2016; Biasutti 2013; James et al. 2015; Dunning et al. 2018; Akinsanola and Zhou 2019c; among others).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "extreme precipitation events",
            "source_entity_type": "Weather_Event",
            "relation": "IMPACTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "West Africa",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "It has been shown that climate change could have robust impacts on agriculture yield (Sultan et al. 2014; Sultan and Gaetani 2016), river flow (Angelina et al. 2015; Aich et al. 2016; Stanzel et al. 2018; Sylla et al. 2018; Sidibe et al. 2020) and extreme precipitation events (Sylla et al. 2015; Han et al. 2019; Akinsanola and Zhou 2019a) over West Africa.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "West African Monsoon",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Sahel",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "In Sahelian countries, around 65% of the labour force (FAO, 2006) and 95% of the land use (Rockstr\u00f6m et al. 2004) are devoted to agriculture, which is predominantly rain-fed. About one-third of the gross domestic product depends on the agricultural sector, versus about 14% for developed nations. The monsoon season occurs between late June to late September (Liebmann et al. 2012; Dunning et al. 2016; Akinsanola and Zhou 2019a) and brings about 80% of the annual rainfall amount. As a result, the Sahelian countries are highly vulnerable to intraseasonal and multidecadal variability of the West African Monsoon.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Hadley cell circulation",
            "source_entity_type": "Teleconnection",
            "relation": "INFLUENCES_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "West Africa",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The warming of the tropical SSTs also impacts the global Hadley cell circulation (Ma et al. 2011, 2018), hence imposing stability and reducing precipitation over the tropics and West Africa.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "rain gauge stations",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "precipitation",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "To evaluate biases in precipitation we use the data of the Global Precipitation Climatology Project (GPCP; Adler et al. 2003) that is available from 1979 to present on a 2.5\u00b0 global grid. GPCP uses data from rain gauge stations, satellites, and sounding observations, which have been merged to estimate monthly precipitation.",
